+++ b/tools/rt-bench.c
@@ -0,0 +1,361 @@
+// rt-bench: GPU time of a WindowServer-like pass on the Intel GPU straight through ANV (no XeMTL in between):
+// a 3840x2400 B8G8R8A8 render target, load op LOAD, LAYERS full-screen triangles of a constant colour blended over it
+// (premultiplied over), random initial content.  The target is, in turn:
+//   optimal tiling in each device memory type, linear tiling in each memory type, and linear tiling on imported host
+//   pages (VK_EXT_external_memory_host, the i915 userptr that IOSurface pages become).
+// So the cost of the IOSurface target splits into layout (optimal vs linear in the same memory) and memory (device
+// memory vs imported pages, both linear).  GPU time from timestamps, median of PASSES.  Read-only.
